  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it or `vite build`, so I haven't seen it render and the layout and framing are untested.\n\n- **Branches:** A seeded mulberry32 routine (seed 7421) builds the layout. It has a 3-segment leaning trunk, 6 major limbs, 18 sub-branches and 36 twigs, so 63 branches in total. Each branch is a tapered cylinder. Same seed gives the same tree.\n- **Base:** There is a flared trunk base and 14 surface roots that dip into the mound.\n- **Foliage:** The crown has 37 sphere clumps of varied size, on the twig tips plus one over the trunk top. They use 4 greens by default. Adding `?season=autumn` to the URL switches the foliage, fallen leaves and grass to autumn colours.\n- **Details:** The trunk has a hollow with a rim and a knot. There are 3 mushrooms and 28 instanced fallen leaves on the mound. A rope swing with a seat hangs from the first limb.\n- **Scene:** The tree sits on a grassy mound with a gradient sky, hemisphere light, a shadow-casting sun and light fog. The orbit camera frames the whole tree and auto-rotates at 0.12 rad/s.\n- **Flags:** After `app.ready()` and one more animation frame, the code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` and `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { ready: true, branchCount: 63, foliageClumpCount: 37, seed: 7421 }`.\n\nI assumed that the primitive `quaternion` option (used to orient branches) and the cylinder `radiusTop`/`radiusBottom` params (used to taper them) are honoured when rendering. The type definitions and the engine source suggest they are. If the branches look wrong when you run it, those are the first things to check.\n\n",
